      },
      "description": "The family's second render: each numeric field gets its own `singleAxis` row, and a `scatter` draws one bubble per observation, sized by value. Sparse, event-shaped data is what this is for — deploys per service, errors per endpoint, jobs per queue. Rows share one time window and one size scale, so ink is comparable both along a row and between rows. Bubble sizes scale by **area** (diameter ∝ √value), so the 20 at 04:30 covers twenty times the ink of the 1 at 02:00, not twenty times the width.",
